  * Image/packaging: stop reserving the large-ring hugepage pool by
    default (#16455). etc/sysctl.d/99-xpf-hugepages.conf shipped
    vm.nr_hugepages = 1440 (2.8 GiB) verbatim through the bake and the
    .deb's /usr/lib/sysctl.d, although the default ring-entries 1024
    needs 5 pages per binding: the 2 GiB Tier-1 validation VM booted
    into OOM kills, a 4 GiB appliance kept ~620 MiB before any service
    started, and systemd's sysctl.d file trigger applied the .deb
    payload at package-install time on foreign hosts. The shipped
    default is now 90 pages (5 x 18 reference bindings at ring 1024);
    bake.py refuses any other shipped default, sizes rig images
    explicitly with --hugepages N (refusing below the 1440-page
    reference large-ring pool), and renders the override onto the
    effective (last-surviving) assignment only. debian/rules installs
    no sysctl.d payload, so apt install on an unmarked host leaves
    /proc/sys/vm/nr_hugepages unchanged. validate.py scenario A
