    as the alias owner, `up` delegates to mouse-target-setup.sh so every
    listener is systemd-pinned (mouse-iperf3@<port>/mouse-echo) instead
    of a detached spawn holding 5201 behind a failed unit, and `down`
    stops units plus orphans. New hermetic mouse-target-setup-selftest
    (wired into run-selftests and test-target-services-lib) pins the
    unit payload; target-services-selftest and cluster-env-selftest
    assert the alias owner/delegation and derivation. Live acceptance
    (reboot the target, .200/.201 + 5200-5211 survive under systemd
    only) remains operator-gated on the loss cluster.
  * Build: inject a command-runner seam into the image validation
    harness (#16196). `Harness` now takes optional `runner`/`popen`
    callables (default: the current subprocess path, stored unresolved
    so uninjected behaviour is unchanged); every child-command site in
    validate.py — the module-level incus/guest helpers via bound
    instance forms, virt-*/qemu-img/`rm`, the QEMU Popen lifetime, and
    the `incus list` re-exec probe — dispatches through the one seam,
    so ownership-refusal and skip-ledger paths are testable with a fake
