  * Config: a literal `apply-groups-except` naming no defined group no
    longer silently no-ops (#16003). The exclusion still removes nothing
    and never errors (a shared cluster config may exclude a group only
    the peer defines), but compilation now warns once per distinct
    unresolved literal name on strict, tolerant, and per-node paths.
    Dynamic `${...}` exclusions stay silent, since another node's view
    may define the group they resolve to there.


