xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * DHCP relay: add bounded per-sender fairness ahead of the
    per-interface aggregate token bucket (#16087, folded 6x on
    #16322). One sender sustaining the maximum-packet-rate no longer
    starves other clients: each chaddr / Client-ID DUID (both peeked
    from the wire, pre-parse) gets a 1/256 share of the rate (floored
    at 1 pps, burst at least 8) in a 256-entry table, with a banked-
    refill waiter rotation so a competing sender progresses even at
    1 pps. No aggregate refund: the aggregate stays the hard
    pre-parse bound and fairness is additional to it. Stops a naive
    single-identity flood; identity rotation still needs switch
    controls (pkg/dhcprelay/README.md).

