    emits a loader-facing token, because swanctl strips the quotes
    then hex/base64-decodes any `0x…`/`0s…` value — so a colliding
    ASCII value (e.g. `0x61626364`) renders base64-armored as
    `secret = "0sMHg2MTYyNjM2NA=="`, which charon decodes back to the
