xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fabric: opt-in link-authentication requirement for zone stamps
    (#16023). `security flow require-authenticated-fabric-stamps` plus
    `chassis cluster fabric-interface-authenticated` /
    `fabric1-interface-authenticated` (operator MACsec/802.1X attestation)
    make the dataplane drop V1/V2 stamps on unattested fabric links as
    Invalid in both split-RG and all-RGs-local placements, closing the
    third-L2-speaker clone of the public FNV zone stamp. Default off
    preserves #10105 document-and-constrain; snapshot protocol v69 fences
    a v68 helper that would ignore the requirement and fail open.


xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sessions: opt-in drop of foreign session hits (#16044).
    `security flow drop-foreign-session-hits` makes the dataplane drop
    a session hit whose arrival zone is not the zone that admitted the
    session, instead of adjudicating it in place under the arrival
    zone's policy and forwarding it on the owner's entry, NAT and
    egress. Default off preserves asymmetric / multi-homed arrival;
    the drop counts in foreign_authority_drops, never revokes the
    session, and host-bound hits stay with the arrival zone's
    host-inbound gate. Snapshot protocol v70 fences a v69 helper that
    would ignore the knob and fail open.
  * Image/day-0: decouple ssh host-key regeneration from the day-0 loader
    (#16445). A new xpf-ssh-hostkeys.service, staged by both the .deb
    (debian/rules) and the bake, runs `ssh-keygen -A` Before=ssh.service
    gated only on host-key absence, so the boot after a failed or
    interrupted zeroize -- whose pending marker occupies the day-0 stamp
    path and skips the loader, while the rotated machine-id defeats
    Ubuntu's first-boot sshd-keygen -- regenerates the erased host keys
    and sshd starts instead of leaving the box console-only. The day-0
    loader keeps its stamp gate (still skipped under the pending
    marker) and no longer runs ssh-keygen. Pinned by
    scripts/image/test_ssh_hostkeys_regen_16445.py (real unit conditions
    evaluated in the failed-reset state, real ssh-keygen -A, sshd -t)
    and the updated test_day0_machine_id_independence_10769.py.
